MockMic
Practice out loud. Walk in ready.
MockMic is a voice-first mock interview practice app. Pick a category, speak or type your answer to an AI-generated question, and get structured, specific feedback on clarity, structure, and one concrete improvement — instantly, no human interviewer required.
Built as a 10-day capstone for the #60DaysOfClaudeAI Challenge by AB Talks.
🚧 Status: Capstone Day 2 of 10 (Challenge Day 52 of 60) — System Design Complete
Production code has not started yet. Day 1 locked the product plan; Day 2 turned that plan into a complete technical blueprint — architecture, database schema, API contracts, screens, and folder structure — so implementation (starting Day 3) can move fast with no redesign mid-build.
Problem
Interview prep tools review resumes and give generic tips, but they rarely make you actually say your answers out loud — which is where most people freeze up in the real thing.
Solution
MockMic simulates the real moment: an AI asks a question, you answer by voice (or typing, if you prefer), and you get feedback built specifically from what you said — not a template.
